cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Beyond AUROC: Quantifying Calibration Collapse in Time-Split
  Validation of Hepatotoxicity and Cardiotoxicity Models
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Noah
    alias: 이노아
version: v0.1
date-released: "2026-10-23"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23583594
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/noahnoah0713/calibration-collapse-time-split"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and results for two FDA toxicity datasets, DILIrank and
  DICTrank. Time-split validation degrades probability calibration far more
  than it degrades discrimination; the cause is decomposed into prevalence
  shift and era shift; and yearly retraining followed by recalibration
  remains effective at label delays of up to five years.
keywords:
  - calibration
  - temporal validation
  - drug-induced liver injury
  - cardiotoxicity
  - distribution shift
  - reproducibility
